    "difficultyReason": "Heavily scaffolded: part a is direct scaling of the cosine range, part b substitutes into 3cos n = n+1 and solves a double linear inequality (the same move as the hinted trig-r10-routine-7, but with the steps split out), and part c asks for a short explanation that the line has y=6 at x=5 while 3cos x ≤ 3. It involves a few linked steps and a graph-to-algebra interpretation, so it is above a single-step recognition or slider-observation task. No unsignposted insight or reframing is needed because each part feeds the next, so it sits below the unhinted, multi-step A3 and the one-part proof in trig-r10-routine-7.",
